  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": "W4 3AP",
  "street_name": "Wellesley Road",
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Major all other major developments",
  "lapsed_date": "05/12/2009",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 3 - The use hereby permitted shall not be begun until details of the arrangements for storing of waste and recycled materials have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.  The arrangements for storing waste and recycled materials shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given and shall be completed before any part of the accommodation hereby permitted is occupied.",
    "Condition : 4 - The use hereby permitted for two (2) self-contained flats shall not be begun until full particulars and details of a scheme to insulate the premises against the transmission of airborne and impact sound between floors and walls has been submitted to an approved by the Local Planning Authority and the development shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given.",
    "Condition : 5 - The conversion of the existing basement to two x two bedrooms flats, the replacement of existing windows throughout the building with double glazed uPVC sash casement windows, and the refurbishment of existing entrance doors of the existing building, as shown on drawing numbers WAT/001, WAT/002, WAT/003, WAT/004 and WAT/005, received 18 September 2006, is satisfactory as the proposal will enhance the appearance of the existing building while the two flats are well located for use of public transport, compatible with the existing use of the building and surrounding properties and provide a satisfactory standard of residential accommodation. The proposed development would also have a nominal impact on the amenity of surrounding properties. Therefore the proposed development complies with the relevant London Borough of Hounslow Unitary Development Plan 2003 policies; ENV-B.1.1 New Development, H.1.1 Location of New Housing Development, H.4.1 Housing Standards and Guidelines and T.1.4 Car and Cycle Parking Facilities for Developments, and the Supplementary Planning Guidance."
  ],
